+# /workspace repo notes
+
+## record/ — the ledger (record.py, test_record.py)
+
+- `record.py` is a stdlib-only CLI; `check-anchors`/`monitor` need `sigstore==4.5.1` and
+  `opentimestamps-client==0.8.0`, which are **not installed in this container**, so
+  `check-anchors` against the real `../ledger` exits 2/1 offline. Anchor checks are exercised in
+  `test_record.py` by monkeypatching `R.check_sigstore` / `R.check_ots` (restore in `finally`).
+- Conventions: data faults raise `Bad` (exit 1), inability to check raises `CantCheck` (exit 2),
+  anything else is caught in `main()` as `FAILURE` (exit 3). Errors print to stderr with a
+  `BAD: `/`CAN'T CHECK: ` prefix and the offending `anchors/NNNNNN.ext` name.
+- Global option `--ledger` must come **before** the subcommand; the tests pass
+  `["--ledger", dir, *args]` to `R.main`.
+- `check-anchors --max-pending-hours H` (added here): with the flag absent, pending OTS proofs are
+  still accepted; with it, a range head whose `check_ots` returns `None` while its Sigstore
+  attestation is older than H hours is `Bad`. Message wording: `still pending N h (...)`.
+- Tests: `cd record && python3 -m unittest test_record` (26 tests; the `rfc8785` one skips when the
+  library is absent). `ResourceWarning`s about unclosed files are pre-existing noise.
+- `record/README.md` is the spec card and tracks the test count, exit-code list, and line counts —
+  keep it in sync with changes.
\ No newline at end of file
